---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../../../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import SiteFooter from '../../../components/SiteFooter.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
	title="Pc Controller privacy policy"
	description="Privacy policy for the Pc Controller Android application."
>
	<SiteHeader />
	<main class="site-main">
		<section class="section">
			<div class="wrap policy">
				<p class="eyebrow">Pc Controller · legal</p>
				<h1 class="section-title">Privacy policy</h1>
				<p class="updated">Effective 17 August 2026</p>

				<div class="policy-summary">
					<strong>Short version:</strong> Pc Controller does not require an account, contain ads,
					use analytics, or send your control activity to SKITZ servers. Device and pairing
					information stays on your Android device.
				</div>

				<section>
					<h2>Information processed by the app</h2>
					<p>
						Pc Controller processes Bluetooth device names and addresses, nearby TV names and IP
						addresses, and remote-control commands so it can connect to devices you select. Samsung
						pairing tokens and TV MAC addresses, LG pairing keys, the last selected TV, and app
						preferences may be stored locally on your Android device.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>How information is used</h2>
					<p>
						This information is used only to discover, pair with, reconnect to, wake, and control
						your own computers and televisions. Commands are sent directly between your phone and
						the selected device over Bluetooth or your local Wi-Fi network.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Information collected by SKITZ</h2>
					<p>
						The Android app does not transmit personal information, pairing credentials, device
						addresses, or control activity to SKITZ. It has no SKITZ account system, advertising,
						analytics, crash-reporting service, or cloud database. App fonts are bundled with the
						install package and are not loaded from Google Fonts or other third-party font services.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Permissions</h2>
					<ul>
						<li><strong>Bluetooth and nearby devices:</strong> connect to and advertise as a Bluetooth HID remote.</li>
						<li><strong>Nearby Wi-Fi and network access:</strong> find and control supported TVs on your local network.</li>
						<li><strong>Notifications and foreground service:</strong> keep an active Bluetooth controller session visible and reliable.</li>
						<li><strong>Legacy location permission on Android 11 and earlier:</strong> required by Android for Bluetooth discovery; Pc Controller does not collect or store your location.</li>
					</ul>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Storage, sharing, and retention</h2>
					<p>
						Locally saved connection information remains on the device until the app is cleared or
						uninstalled. Pc Controller does not sell or share this information with SKITZ or data
						brokers. The app communicates with the computers and TVs you explicitly choose to
						control.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Children</h2>
					<p>
						Pc Controller is a general utility and is not directed to children. It does not
						knowingly collect personal information from children.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Security</h2>
					<p>
						Pairing credentials remain in Android app storage. Some television protocols use local
						network HTTP or self-signed certificates because that is what the television provides.
						Use Pc Controller only on a trusted home or private network.
					</p>
				</section>

				<section>
					<h2>Changes and contact</h2>
					<p>
						This policy may be updated when app behavior changes. Questions about this policy can
						be sent to <a href="mailto:toonersai@gmail.com">toonersai@gmail.com</a>.
					</p>
				</section>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
	<SiteFooter />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
	.policy {
		max-width: 48rem;
	}

	.updated {
		margin: -0.6rem 0 1.4rem;
		color: var(--muted);
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
	}

	.policy-summary {
		margin-bottom: 2rem;
		padding: 1.1rem 1.2rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--line);
		background: var(--paper-2);
		font-family: var(--font-type);
		line-height: 1.6;
	}

	.policy section {
		margin-top: 1.75rem;
	}

	.policy h2 {
		margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
		font-family: var(--font-display);
		font-size: 1.25rem;
	}

	.policy p,
	.policy li {
		color: var(--ink);
		font-family: var(--font-type);
		line-height: 1.65;
	}

	.policy p {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.policy ul {
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.55rem;
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
	}

	.policy a {
		color: inherit;
		text-decoration-thickness: 2px;
		text-underline-offset: 3px;
	}
</style>
